Relevant columns & how they will be used
----------------------------------------

bigquery-public-data.sunroof_solar.solar_potential_by_postal_code  
• `state_name` : grouping key (state level aggregation)  
• `count_qualified` : # of buildings suitable for solar (part of “gap” calc)  
• `percent_covered` : average % of Google‑Maps rooftop area analysed (needed for “gap” calc)  
• `percent_qualified` : average % of analysed area that is suitable (needed for “gap” calc)  
• `number_of_panels_total` : potential panel count (sum)  
• `kw_total` : total kW capacity (sum)  
• `yearly_sunlight_kwh_total` : total annual generation (sum)  
• `carbon_offset_metric_tons` : potential CO₂ offset (sum)  
• `existing_installs_count` : estimated bldgs already having solar (sum)  

bigquery-public-data.sunroof_solar.solar_potential_by_censustract  
(Same fields – duplicated purpose, used to repeat the calculations at census‑tract granularity.)  

Conditions that will be repeatedly used  
• `GROUP BY state_name` – to roll every metric to state level  
• `WHERE state_name IS NOT NULL` – defensive filter  
• `LIMIT 20` – show only first 20 states in sample outputs  


Ten progressively‑richer example queries
----------------------------------------

```sql
-- 1) List all distinct states (postal‑code table)
SELECT DISTINCT `state_name`
FROM `bigquery-public-data.sunroof_solar.solar_potential_by_postal_code`
WHERE state_name IS NOT NULL
ORDER BY state_name
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 2) How many ZIP codes are captured for each state?
SELECT state_name,
       COUNT(*) AS zip_cnt
FROM `bigquery-public-data.sunroof_solar.solar_potential_by_postal_code`
GROUP BY state_name
ORDER BY zip_cnt DESC
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 3) Total qualified buildings by state (postal level)
SELECT state_name,
       SUM(count_qualified) AS qualified_buildings_zip
FROM `bigquery-public-data.sunroof_solar.solar_potential_by_postal_code`
GROUP BY state_name
ORDER BY qualified_buildings_zip DESC
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 4) Same metric but at census‑tract level
SELECT state_name,
       SUM(count_qualified) AS qualified_buildings_tract
FROM `bigquery-public-data.sunroof_solar.solar_potential_by_censustract`
GROUP BY state_name
ORDER BY qualified_buildings_tract DESC
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 5) Average Google‑Maps coverage & suitability by state (postal level)
SELECT state_name,
       AVG(percent_covered)   AS avg_pct_covered_zip,
       AVG(percent_qualified) AS avg_pct_suitable_zip
FROM `bigquery-public-data.sunroof_solar.solar_potential_by_postal_code`
GROUP BY state_name
ORDER BY state_name
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 6) Join postal & tract aggregations side‑by‑side on state
WITH zip AS (
  SELECT state_name,
         SUM(count_qualified) AS qualified_zip,
         AVG(percent_covered) AS pct_cov_zip,
         AVG(percent_qualified) AS pct_suit_zip
  FROM `bigquery-public-data.sunroof_solar.solar_potential_by_postal_code`
  GROUP BY state_name
),
tract AS (
  SELECT state_name,
         SUM(count_qualified) AS qualified_tr,
         AVG(percent_covered) AS pct_cov_tr,
         AVG(percent_qualified) AS pct_suit_tr
  FROM `bigquery-public-data.sunroof_solar.solar_potential_by_censustract`
  GROUP BY state_name
)
SELECT z.state_name,
       qualified_zip, pct_cov_zip, pct_suit_zip,
       qualified_tr,  pct_cov_tr,  pct_suit_tr
FROM zip z
JOIN tract t
ON z.state_name = t.state_name
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 7) Potential‑installation GAP at postal‑code level
SELECT state_name,
       SUM(count_qualified)                                             AS qualified_zip,
       SUM(existing_installs_count)                                     AS current_installs,
       SUM(count_qualified)/AVG(percent_qualified/100)/AVG(percent_covered/100)
         AS potential_total_bldgs,
       (SUM(count_qualified)/AVG(percent_qualified/100)/AVG(percent_covered/100))
         - SUM(existing_installs_count)                                 AS gap_zip
FROM `bigquery-public-data.sunroof_solar.solar_potential_by_postal_code`
GROUP BY state_name
ORDER BY gap_zip DESC
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 8) Potential‑installation GAP at census‑tract level
SELECT state_name,
       SUM(count_qualified)                                             AS qualified_tr,
       SUM(existing_installs_count)                                     AS current_installs,
       SUM(count_qualified)/AVG(percent_qualified/100)/AVG(percent_covered/100)
         AS potential_total_bldgs,
       (SUM(count_qualified)/AVG(percent_qualified/100)/AVG(percent_covered/100))
         - SUM(existing_installs_count)                                 AS gap_tr
FROM `bigquery-public-data.sunroof_solar.solar_potential_by_censustract`
GROUP BY state_name
ORDER BY gap_tr DESC
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 9) Compare postal vs census gaps in a single view
WITH p AS (
  SELECT state_name,
         (SUM(count_qualified)/AVG(percent_qualified/100)/AVG(percent_covered/100))
           - SUM(existing_installs_count) AS gap_zip
  FROM `bigquery-public-data.sunroof_solar.solar_potential_by_postal_code`
  GROUP BY state_name
), c AS (
  SELECT state_name,
         (SUM(count_qualified)/AVG(percent_qualified/100)/AVG(percent_covered/100))
           - SUM(existing_installs_count) AS gap_tr
  FROM `bigquery-public-data.sunroof_solar.solar_potential_by_censustract`
  GROUP BY state_name
)
SELECT p.state_name, gap_zip, gap_tr
FROM p
JOIN c USING(state_name)
ORDER BY gap_zip DESC
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 10) FINAL comprehensive state comparison (postal vs census)
WITH postal AS (
  SELECT state_name,
         SUM(count_qualified)                              AS qualified_zip,
         AVG(percent_covered)                              AS avg_pct_cov_zip,
         AVG(percent_qualified)                            AS avg_pct_suit_zip,
         SUM(number_of_panels_total)                       AS panels_zip,
         SUM(kw_total)                                     AS kw_zip,
         SUM(yearly_sunlight_kwh_total)                    AS kwh_zip,
         SUM(carbon_offset_metric_tons)                    AS co2_zip,
         SUM(existing_installs_count)                      AS current_zip,
         (SUM(count_qualified)
           /AVG(percent_qualified/100)/AVG(percent_covered/100))
           - SUM(existing_installs_count)                  AS gap_zip
  FROM `bigquery-public-data.sunroof_solar.solar_potential_by_postal_code`
  GROUP BY state_name
),
tract AS (
  SELECT state_name,
         SUM(count_qualified)                              AS qualified_tr,
         AVG(percent_covered)                              AS avg_pct_cov_tr,
         AVG(percent_qualified)                            AS avg_pct_suit_tr,
         SUM(number_of_panels_total)                       AS panels_tr,
         SUM(kw_total)                                     AS kw_tr,
         SUM(yearly_sunlight_kwh_total)                    AS kwh_tr,
         SUM(carbon_offset_metric_tons)                    AS co2_tr,
         SUM(existing_installs_count)                      AS current_tr,
         (SUM(count_qualified)
           /AVG(percent_qualified/100)/AVG(percent_covered/100))
           - SUM(existing_installs_count)                  AS gap_tr
  FROM `bigquery-public-data.sunroof_solar.solar_potential_by_censustract`
  GROUP BY state_name
)
SELECT p.state_name,

       -- Postal‑code level metrics
       qualified_zip, avg_pct_cov_zip, avg_pct_suit_zip,
       panels_zip, kw_zip, kwh_zip, co2_zip, current_zip, gap_zip,

       -- Census‑tract level metrics
       qualified_tr,  avg_pct_cov_tr,  avg_pct_suit_tr,
       panels_tr, kw_tr, kwh_tr, co2_tr, current_tr, gap_tr

FROM postal p
JOIN tract  t
ON p.state_name = t.state_name
ORDER BY p.state_name
LIMIT 20;
```

